      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given the polynomials \\( f(x) \\) and \\( g(x) \\) such that \\( f(x) + g(x) = -2 + x \\), we need to find \\( g(x) \\) given that \\( f(x) = x^3 - 2x - 2 \\).\n\nFirst, substitute \\( f(x) \\) into the given equation:\n\\[\nf(x) + g(x) = -2 + x\n\\]\n\\[\n(x^3 - 2x - 2) + g(x) = -2 + x\n\\]\n\nNext, isolate \\( g(x) \\) by subtracting \\( f(x) \\) from both sides of the equation:\n\\[\ng(x) = (-2 + x) - (x^3 - 2x - 2)\n\\]\n\nSimplify the right-hand side:\n\\[\ng(x) = -2 + x - x^3 + 2x + 2\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\ng(x) = -x^3 + x + x - 2 + 2\n\\]\n\\[\ng(x) = -x^3 + 2x\n\\]\n\nThus, the polynomial \\( g(x) \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-x^3 + 2x}\n\\]",
