      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find \\( g(x) \\) given that \\( f(x) + g(x) = -2 + x \\) and \\( f(x) = x^3 - 2x - 2 \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\( f(x) \\) into the equation \\( f(x) + g(x) = -2 + x \\).\n2. Solve for \\( g(x) \\).\n\nLet's start by substituting \\( f(x) \\) into the equation:\n\n\\[ f(x) + g(x) = -2 + x \\]\n\\[ (x^3 - 2x - 2) + g(x) = -2 + x \\]\n\nNext, we isolate \\( g(x) \\) by subtracting \\( f(x) \\) from both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ g(x) = (-2 + x) - (x^3 - 2x - 2) \\]\n\nNow, we simplify the right-hand side:\n\n\\[ g(x) = -2 + x - x^3 + 2x + 2 \\]\n\\[ g(x) = -x^3 + 3x \\]\n\nSo, the polynomial \\( g(x) \\) is:\n\n\\[ g(x) = -x^3 + 3x \\]\n\nLet's verify this solution using Python code to ensure its accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\r\n\r\n# Define the variable\r\nx = symbols('x')\r\n\r\n# Define the given polynomials f(x) and the equation f(x) + g(x) = -2 + x\r\nf_x = x**3 - 2*x - 2\r\ng_x = symbols('g_x')\r\n\r\n# Define the equation f(x) + g(x) = -2 + x\r\nequation = Eq(f_x + g_x, -2 + x)\r\n\r\n# Solve for g(x)\r\nsolution = solve(equation, g_x)\r\nprint(solution)\n```\n```output\n[-x**3 + 3*x]\n```\nThe solution obtained from the code confirms our manual calculation. Therefore, the polynomial \\( g(x) \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-x^3 + 3x}\n\\]",
